i.com】\\nL818:   * 【500†Codex for Students†developers.openai.com】\\nL819:   * 【501†Codex for Open Source†developers.openai.com】\\nL820:   * 【502†Events†luma.com】\\nL821: \\nL822: ### Blog\\nL823: \\nL824:   * 【503†Company blog†openai.com】\\nL825:   * 【504†Developer blog†developers.openai.com】\\nL826: \\nL827: 【505†Showcase】 [Button: Blog ][Button: Cookbook ][Button: Learn ][Button: Community ]\\nL828: \\nL829: Docs Showcase\\nL830: \\nL831:   * 【506†All posts】\\nL875: ### Topics\\nL876: \\nL877:   * 【534†Agents】\\nL878:   * 【535†Audio & Voice】\\nL879:   * 【536†Computer Use】\\nL880:   * 【537†Codex】\\nL881:   * 【538†Evals】\\nL882:   * 【539†gpt-oss】\\nL883:   * 【540†Fine-tuning】\\nL884:   * 【541†Image generation】\\nL885:   * 【542†Scaling】\\nL886:   * 【543†Tools】\\nL887:   * 【544†Video generation】\\nL888: \\nL889:   * 【545†Community】\\nL890: \\nL891: ### Programs\\nL892: \\nL893:   * 【546†Codex Ambassadors】\\nL894:     * 【547†Meet the ambassadors】\\nL895:   * 【548†Codex for Students】\\nL896:   * 【549†Student Collective†openai.com】\\nL897:   * 【550†Codex for Open Source】\\nL898:   * 【551†OpenAI for Startups†openai.com】\\nL899: ### Spaces\\nL900: \\nL901:   * 【502†Events†luma.com】\\nL902:   * 【552†Developer Forum†community.openai.com】\\nL903:   * 【553†Discord†discord.com】\\nL904:   * 【554†Reddit†www.reddit.com】\\nL905:   * 【555†X†x.com】\\nL906: \\nL907: 【556†API Dashboard†platform.openai.com】\\nL908: \\nL909: 【557†Try ChatGPT†chatgpt.com】\\nL910: \\nL911:   * 【4†Home】\\nL912: \\nL913: ### Get started\\nL914: \\nL915:   * 【308†Quickstart】\\nL916:   * 【309†Use ChatGPT】\\nL917:   * 【310†Get started with Work】\\nL918:   * 【311†Meet dots】\\nL919:   * 【312†Import from another agent】\\nL920: ### Foundations\\nL921: \\nL922:   * 【313†Prompting】\\nL923:   * 【314†Working with agents】\\nL924:   * 【315†Model selection】\\nL925:   * 【316†Personalize ChatGPT】\\nL926:   * 【317†Skills & Plugins】\\nL927:   * 【318†Permissions】\\nL928: \\nL929: ### Explore\\nL930: \\nL931:   * 【319†What's new】\\nL932:   * 【320†Models】\\nL933:   * 【321†Pricing】\\nL934:   * 【322†Glossary】\\nL935: \\nL936: ### Available on\\nL937: \\nL938:   * 【323†ChatGPT desktop app】\\nL939:   * 【324†ChatGPT mobile app】\\nL940:   * 【325†ChatGPT on the web】\\nL941:   * 【326†Codex CLI】\\nL942:   * 【327†Codex IDE extension】\\nL943:   * 【328†Codex Cloud】\\nL944: ### Releases\\nL945: \\nL946:   * 【329†Changelog】\\nL947:   * 【330†Feature Maturity】\\nL948:   * 【331†Open Source】\\nL949: \\nL950: Codex CLI\\nL951: # Inspect, edit, and run code from your terminal\\nL952: \\nL953: Inspect code, make changes, run commands, and automate repeatable work without leaving your terminal.\\nL954: \\nL955: 【558†Install Codex】\\nL956: \\nL957: 【559†CLI reference】\\nL958: $ codex\\nL959: \\nL960:     ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\\nL961:     │ >_ OpenAI Codex                                  │\\nL962:     │                                                  │\\nL963:     │ model:     gpt-6.1-sol medium/model to change │\\nL964:     │ directory: ~/code                                │\\nL965:     ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\\nL966: \\nL967:       To get started, describe a task or try one of these commands:\\nL968: \\nL969:       /init - create an AGENTS.md file with instructions for Codex\\nL970:       /status - show current session configuration\\nL971:       /permissions - choose what Codex is allowed to do\\nL972:       /model - choose what model and reasoning effort to use\\nL973:       /review - review any changes and find issues\\nL974: \\nL975: \\nL976: \\nL977:     › Refactor the Dashboard component to React Hooks\\nL978: \\nL979: \\nL980:       100% context left · ? for shortcuts\\nL981: 01\\nL982: ## Work against your local repository\\nL983: \\nL984: Let Codex inspect files, make edits, and run the tools already installed on your machine.\\nL985: \\nL986: 02\\nL987: \\nL988: ## Stay in control\\nL989: \\nL990: Choose the model, reasoning effort, permissions, and commands that fit the task.\\nL991: \\nL992: 03\\nL993: \\nL994: ## Compose with scripts and CI\\nL995: \\nL996: Use Codex interactively or call codex exec from repeatable workflows and pipelines.\\nL997: \\nL998: Quickstart\\nL999: \\nL1000: ## Get started with Codex CLI\\nL1001: \\nL1002: Install Codex, sign in, and run your first task from a project directory.\\nL1003: \\nL1004:   1. 1\\nL1005: ### Install Codex\\nL1006: \\nL1007: macOS/Linux Windows npm Homebrew\\nL1008: \\nL1009: Install the Codex CLI with the standalone installer for macOS and Linux.\\nL1010: \\nL1011: Install Codex\\nL1012: \\nL1013:     `curl -fsSL https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.sh | sh`\\nL1014: \\nL1015: Update Codex\\nL1016: \\nL1017:     `curl -fsSL https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.sh | sh`\\nL1018: \\nL1019:   2. 2\\nL1020: \\nL1021: ### Run Codex and sign in\\nL1022: \\nL1023: Open a project directory and run `codex`. The first time you run Codex, choose Sign in with ChatGPT or another available sign-in method.\\nL1024: \\nL1025: 【453†Review authentication options】\\nL1026: \\nL1027:   3. 3\\nL1028: ### Start your first task\\nL1029: \\nL1030: Describe what you want to accomplish. For example, ask Codex to explain the project, make a focused change, or help debug an issue.\\nL1031: \\nL1032: `Tell me about this project`\\nL1033: \\nL1034: Create Git checkpoints before and after a task so you can revert changes. See the 【560†best practices】.\\nL1035: \\nL1036: Next steps\\nL1037: \\nL1038:   * 【559†Explore the CLI reference】\\nL1039:   * 【561†Configure Codex】\\nL1040:   * 【403†Automate with codex exec】\\nL1041: ## See what Codex CLI can do\\nL1042: \\nL1043: Use one focused terminal loop for interactive work, automation, review, and delegation.\\nL1044: \\nL1045: 01\\nL1046: ### Keep the coding loop in your terminal\\nL1047: \\nL1048: Start Codex in a repository to explore unfamiliar code, plan a change, edit files, and run your local development tools. Steer the active turn, inspect commands and diffs as they appear, and keep follow-up work in the same session.\\nL1049: \\nL1050: 【559†Learn more】\\nL1051: \\nL1052: >_OpenAI Codex(v0.143.0)\\nL1053: \\nL1054: model:gpt-6.1-sol medium /model to change directory:~/code/my-app\\nL1055: \\nL1056: 02\\nL1057: ### Use skills and plugins\\nL1058: \\nL1059: Package repeatable instructions as skills, then add plugins to connect Codex to your team's tools and data without leaving the CLI.\\nL1060: \\nL1061: 【562†Learn more】\\nL1062: \\nL1063: zsh — plugins\\nL1064: \\nL1065: Plugins\\nL1066: \\nL1067: Browse plugins from available marketplaces.\\nL1068: \\nL1069: Installed 17 of 1751 available plugins.\\nL1070: \\n\"}}\n{\"i\":3,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"e0607b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.2956357,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":138,\"output\":\"{\\\"path\\\": \\\"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\Diego Tapia\\\\\\\\.codex\\\\\\\\sessions\\\\\\\\2026\\\\\\\\10\\\\\\\\19\\\\\\\\rollout-2026-10-19T23-06-45-01a1570f-a3cd-7de3-9846-8bfc7596f2ee.jsonl\\\", \\\"size\\\": 7613141, \\\"id\\\": \\\"01a1570f-a3cd-7de3-9846-8bfc7596f2ee\\\", \\\"cwd\\\": \\\"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\Diego Tapia\\\\\\\\Desktop\\\\\\\\Pene\\\\\\\\U\\\\\\\\Tesis\\\\\\\\tesis_karaoke\\\"}\\r\\n{\\\"path\\\": \\\"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\Diego Tapia\\\\\\\\.codex\\\\\\\\sessions\\\\\\\\2026\\\\\\\\11\\\\\\\\14\\\\\\\\rollout-2026-11-14T16-26-36-01a1db86-a51a-7763-8f16-5a729e09225d.jsonl\\\", \\\"size\\\": 917304, \\\"id\\\": \\\"01a1db86-a51a-7763-8f16-5a729e09225d\\\", \\\"cwd\\\": \\\"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\Diego Tapia\\\\\\\\Desktop\\\\\\\\Pene\\\\\\\\U\\\\\\\\Tesis\\\\\\\\tesis_karaoke\\\"}\\r\\n\"}}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1dbc1-59c0-7a41-a30f-7c85c2fa1732","create_time":1794688623.97875}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"complete","sources":[{"plugin_id":"unified-computer-use@openai-